  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Compute $P(0\\le X<1)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3},\\, & 0\\le x<2, \\\\ \\frac{1}{5}x & 2\\le x\\le 3, \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise.}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "worked_solution": "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a\\le X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(0\\le X<1) & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{8}{x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{32}{x}^{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}({1}^{4}-{0}^{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{32}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
